## Cover a cyclic staffing schedule

Exercise files: [instance-03.lp](../assets/shifts/instances/instance-03.lp) · [shifts.lp](../assets/shifts/shifts.lp) · [instance-03.json](../assets/shifts/solutions/instance-03.json).

```elixir
workdir = Course.workspace(Path.expand("../assets/shifts", __DIR__))
```

Choose at most the allowed number of distinct start/length shifts. Their starts and lengths must fit an input shift type. Each shift repeats daily with a positive staffing level that may vary by day. Coverage wraps through the final day back to the first. At every slot, staffing must stay within the permitted excess and shortage.

Complete the starter encoding before comparing its projected models with the supplied solution data.

### Keep the data contract

Read `day/1`, `slot/1`, `emp/3`, `type/4`, `exceed/1`, `shorten/1` and `maxshifts/1`. Show `shift(Start,Length,Day,Employees)`. Every chosen start/length pair needs one staffing atom per day. This exercise bounds shift count rather than introducing an unstated optimization objective.

### Complete the model

Implement the conditions in the problem description without hard-coding an instance. Keep the required show signature so results can be compared with the reference data.

### Develop and check the encoding

Complete the editable encoding below. Compare its shown atom sets with the JSON answers in `solutions`; `optimal_cost` records a proven optimum when present. Download your edits before cleanup.

